Add the 3dfx Voodoo 2 device's meson subdir (hw/voodoo, overlaid from
voodoo/ by prepare-qemu.sh; doc 21, M14). The device is `-device voodoo2`,
a PCI function nothing instantiates by default; the directory's own
meson.build builds 86Box's rasterizer as a static library against the
shim of 86Box's headers and adds the QEMU device to the i386 sourceset.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index cb7dba1..d1e0f2a 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -3701,6 +3701,7 @@ if have_system or have_user
   subdir('hw/3dfx')
   subdir('hw/mesa')
   subdir('hw/d3dpt')
+  subdir('hw/voodoo')
 endif
 
 subdir('audio')
